    "turn_idx": 121,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and I suppose, too, it's something that we should all be aware of about what institutions the left is most interested in. They've taken on the big ones, things that we didn't think they could take on. Major corporations now, too. That's what's interesting to me. The newspapers were always liberal. They weren't left wing. News Media was always liberal. It wasn't less left-wing. And so they have marched through not only obviously journalism and academia, but now the businesses, major businesses. And this DEI thing that people like Bill Ackman are going after and that are trying to do the uncovering of that the way that people like Matt Teiby and Alex Behrenson and Michael Schellenberger were doing with social media. They resist that for Hammer and Tongue because they know that we're on to them.",
